# Host and environment adapters

Apply only the rows relevant to the selected skill.

- **Subagents.** Translate upstream `Agent`, `Task`, background-agent, and
  `subagent_type` wording to the host's real collaboration tools. If independent
  parallel reviewers are part of the promised result and the host cannot
  provide them, report `blocked/tool_unavailable`; never fabricate their
  outputs. Sequential work is acceptable only when independence is not part of
  the promise.
- **Trackers and remote services.** Use only a tracker actually configured for
  the project. Creating, editing, closing, or commenting on remote items needs
  authorization from the request. When the upstream module permits a local
  artifact, prefer that at an unapproved remote-write boundary.
- **Local specs, tickets, and maps.** If the request authorizes a project-local
  artifact but forbids or does not configure a remote tracker, use the donor's
  local convention without running the full setup interview:
  `.scratch/<feature>/spec.md`, `.scratch/<feature>/issues/`, or
  `.scratch/<effort>/map.md`. State the chosen slug. An explicit destination
  from the user or project overrides this default.
- **Git completion.** Instructions to stage everything, commit, push, finish a
  merge/rebase, create branches, or never abort are subordinate to the user's
  requested scope and the current repository's rules.
- **Implementation review before commit.** Capture the pre-change `HEAD` before
  implementation. A `code-review` of work in progress must cover both the
  committed range from that fixed point and the current index/worktree,
  including untracked files; `git diff <fixed-point>...HEAD` alone is not the
  review input. Give both independent reviewers the same complete change set.
  This allows an authorized `implement` flow to honor “do not commit” without
  silently reviewing an empty diff.
- **`git-guardrails-claude-code`.** Use only for Claude Code. The projected hook
  is patched to require `python3` and fail closed when the dependency or valid
  JSON input is missing. Verify one blocked dangerous command and one allowed
  harmless command before claiming installation succeeded.
- **Gemini CLI.** The global installer writes a dedicated projection under
  `${GEMINI_CLI_HOME:-$HOME}/.gemini/skills` and adds selector-only leaf names
  to Gemini's user `skills.disabled` list. It preserves user-owned values and,
  after schema-2 ownership has been established, removes only obsolete values
  that this installer added. A user-reenabled value is not added back. Legacy
  schema-1 removal requires an explicit, preflighted reconciliation flag.
  A disabled leaf is read through this selector's loader; host activation still
  requires Gemini's consent. Additional user or admin disables can reduce the
  enabled set. If another user or workspace skill shadows these installed
  directories, stop rather than claiming this bundle was loaded.
- **`scaffold-exercises`.** Verify the AI Hero lint command and its package
  manager exist before scaffolding. Do not claim lint success when unavailable.
- **`claude-handoff`.** Requires a Claude host whose CLI supports background
  agents. A background child must inherit this skill bundle. When the
  current session was loaded with `--plugin-dir`, include
  `--plugin-dir "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}"` in the spawned `claude --bg` command;
  if bundle inheritance cannot be verified, use `handoff` instead and report
  the detour. On non-Claude hosts, use `handoff` rather than impersonating a
  Claude lane.
- **`wizard`.** Treat `.env`, GitHub secrets, browser launches, and third-party
  account changes as separate permission boundaries. Never echo secret values.
  Accept environment keys only when they match
  `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*`; if the template cannot preserve multiline or
  special-character values without corruption, stop as
  `blocked/criterion_unmet` instead of writing them.
- **Experimental and legacy modules.** Preserve their distinct behavior, but
  disclose the lifecycle label before relying on it for a material side effect.

