### Coalition-context coverage

There were 4,211 context-bearing rows and 15,569 context-free rows among 19,780 legal catalogue rows. The pooled `contexts.get(...) is None` fraction was **78.7108%**. Across anchors it was min / q25 / median / q75 / max / mean = **78.1347% / 78.5729% / 78.7769% / 78.9014% / 79.1751% / 78.7079%**. This is 0.4532 percentage points below the supplied C3REACH value of 79.164% and confirms the same sparse interaction-forward regime.

### Head provenance and shape

No training was run. Q1 and Q2 for all five arms came from the existing epoch-2000 checkpoints for learner seed `5166716249291843642`. Their shapes were Q1 `16→8→1` and Q2 `22→100→50→50→1`.

The available epoch-2000 C3 checkpoints are `117→64→64→1`, but the current deployed `CoalitionContext.invariant_vector(member_width=38)` is 240-wide. Attempting the checkpoint produced a verified matrix-shape exception (`117 != 240`) before any anchor result was accepted. For the successful latency run, each arm therefore used a deterministic **untrained synthetic C3 head of the correct deployed shape `240→64→64→1`**, with the same scalar ReLU forward implementation. The assertion checked width 240 on every context-bearing anchor. This is shape-honest for the requested forward-pass cost; the learned values are irrelevant to that cost.

The synthetic C3 values can affect which configurations the five arms select and hence how many distinct configurations the committed physical batch deduplicates. Accordingly, the physical-evaluation stage above is exactly measured for these synthetic-head selections, not attributed to an unavailable deployable trained C3 checkpoint.

