/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:113:- **D-MIN-5 (now measured, previously zero-by-construction). C2 tie frequency.** The build-3 code had no C2 tie-break and the field was hard-coded `False`. This pilot implemented the smallest schema-satisfying measurement: the fraction of non-incumbent (user, action) candidates whose FULL-arm C2 head score exactly equals the incumbent's. Measured value: **0.0** on both catalogue anchors (`c2_tie_frequency` 0.0, `c2_tie_pair_fraction_mean` 0.0). The C2 head discriminates every candidate; the zero is now an observation rather than an artefact, but it is still a proxy for head indiscriminability, not for a build-3 tie-break code path.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:115:- **D-MIN-7 (scope). Statistical power is nil.** 5 anchors x 1 carrier x 2 learner seeds = 10 FULL decisions per catalogue anchor. No interval, no seed-variance estimate and no contrast in this report is powered. The g_A/g_I quantiles below are computed over 10 points and p05/p95 coincide with min/max.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:117:- **D-MIN-9 (schema shortcut). `top_choice_agreement` differs sharply by catalogue anchor** (0.5 on `P-a0`, 0.0 on `P-u`) with no obvious mechanism at this sample size; recorded so it is checked, not explained.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:133:- Exact S0 over 48 boundaries for every catalogue profile was unbounded in the joined engine. The pilot ranks S0's top-two proposals with provider-primitive C1+C2, applies the same bounded evacuation rule, evaluates that set with exact nominal boundary-0 physics, then evaluates the committed S0 profile over all 48 realised boundaries.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/V025-PILOT-MIN-REPORT-2026-09-09.md:134:- Exhaustive exact interaction decomposition over every catalogue row was also unbounded. Exact Psi is computed for every P-u joint escape candidate and every selected FULL coalition; other rows retain learned scoring only. P-u top-10 users are primitive-ranked by |d_i^u|. The pilot S_UNI wall budget was reduced to 5 seconds, with the engine's fallback and termination certificate retained verbatim.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:7:A2. **I_coordinator** (per anchor): global nominal geometry with beam-specific cross gains, all users' legal sets, b⁻, the reference proposal a⁰, the bounded catalogue 𝒞 (decision 4/CB-2), the nominal model 𝓜 (no realised fading, no future TLE beyond the declared forecast horizon), and the outputs of 𝓜 for each profile in 𝒞 (joint load, coupled powers, interference, activation, service, bits, energy, continuation). Compute = the declared budget (§F).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:9:A4. **Equalised between FULL and every DROP/comparator arm:** primitive access and timestamps, forecast method, physical identities, catalogue construction (authenticated identical catalogues at matched anchors), joint search, guards, tie-breaking, validation, deadline, fallback. Any learned pruning is part of the declared intervention. An exact evaluator may never reinsert a removed score through ranking, pruning or a score-dependent guard.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:20:C2. **C3 learner form:** a **set-conditioned scalar interaction head** Ψ̂_θ(Z_t, a⁰, A, a_A): permutation-invariant over A, anchored Ψ̂(∅) = Ψ̂({u}) = 0, trained on the residual Ψ_A / κ over the coalition support of the bounded catalogue; deployed S3 optimises the **complete** score C1 + C2 + Ψ̂ over 𝒞 with the sealed service guard, budget and fallback. S0 = the same selector with the exact Ψ_A in place of Ψ̂. S_UNI = iterated exact unilateral improvement to a local optimum (every legal unilateral alternative evaluated with the same nominal joint physics at each iterate, deterministic improving move, atomic commit of the final profile only, termination certificate reported).
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:24:C6. **Zero results are allowed and informative:** a zero C3 source marginal ends the positive C3 claim under this scope; an interval excluding the practical margin supports "no practically relevant benefit"; a lower-bound failure alone is inconclusive; neither permits changing features, catalogues, sources or regimes until C3 becomes positive.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1-2026-09-08.md:40:F3. **Capability manifest fields:** telemetry sources and ages, roster and cross-gain coverage, model assumptions and calibration source, worker hardware/count, catalogue bounds, solver limits, memory, missing-data handling, measured end-to-end latency distribution.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:9:The strongest defense is documented. The [v1.1 amendment](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-08.md:6) calls 50 Mbit/s a *nominal*, synthetic operating point, expressly permits partial delivery, credits achieved full-buffer ACM bits and separates PHY service from target attainment. The [original declaration](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-2026-09-08.md:14) declares no guaranteed-rate endpoint. Most decisively, [v1.9 §1](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-probe-ws/.scratch/multi-catfish-v025-physics-successor/V025-PHYSICS-SUCCESSOR-PRIORITY-DECLARATION-v1.9-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:5) explicitly requires: **“The margin must not be re-solved into transmit power.”** It fixes nominal powers, applies the quantile only to wanted-link predicted reception, and objects specifically to increased interference and changed cap feasibility. The proposed change reverses that instruction.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:13:The arithmetic against this convention remains severe. For a feasible uncapped fixed point, nominal SINR is approximately `Γ(n)`. At occupancy one, `Γ(1)` is the table floor, so `qΓ(1)` falls below every mode when the de-rating exceeds the negligible numerical clearance. The reported 9.16e−9 dB headroom cannot accommodate a 1.1–4.8 dB de-rating. The policy can therefore spend energy on a singleton while selecting no mode. Its universal singleton rejection need not have been anticipated merely because its constituent rules were deliberate.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:65:The replacement cost extends far beyond changing two provisioning sites and their dense twins. Every successor result depending on RF power, coupled interference, caps, modes, bits, energy, service, occupancy or EE requires regeneration. Search paths and catalogues change, so old selected assignments cannot simply be rescored and called new optima. Physics-dependent observations, forecasts and C1/C2/C3 labels need regeneration; affected learned heads need retraining; learned trajectories, contrasts, uncertainty intervals and admission decisions need new evaluation. Calibration diagnostics must be recomputed while keeping the frozen price for this comparison; changing the price would introduce another model decision.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:111:I tested the claim that retaining the target mode establishes 90% availability. At an uncapped corrected nominal fixed point, with desired-link fading factor `F_d`,
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:119:Finally, 2,000 means twenty user-anchor populations of 100, not 2,000 independent people; the 12,000 sweep results reuse users, steps and arms across five widths. Transmission counts additionally repeat boundaries and slot subdivisions. They are census denominators, not independent samples establishing narrow confidence bounds. The searches maximise fixed-price `B − η_ref E` at boundary zero and commit across 48 boundaries, with a bounded joint catalogue and no deployment deadline in these diagnostics. A positive selection certificate need not imply a positive committed EE gap. The [per-user metric report](/home/sat/mcrl-v023-codex-audits/parallel-20260909/PER-USER-METRIC-2026-09-10.md) preserves the pooled gap's sign under both energy allocations, so changing attribution does not rescue the negative narrow-width result. None of these diagnostics establishes a population-wide, learned or deployable coordination claim.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PROVISIONING-ADVERSARIAL-2026-09-10.md:121:If the change proceeds, preserve the original declared primary, seals, source, receipts, figures and unfavorable findings as results of the nominal-power convention, and explicitly state that the successor reverses v1.9's deliberate policy to pursue target-mode selection at the existing design percentile; disclose that all reported outcomes were known before this decision and make the rationale independent of C3's sign. Freeze the existing 1.66° one-sided beam width, constants, thresholds, signs, seeds, horizons, price, service guard and acceptance rules for the provisioning comparison; give any antenna change its own design decision, retain every already observed width as exploratory, and never promote a positive width to erase the original primary result. Specify and review the numerical clearance algorithm at every affected scalar and dense site, then regenerate all affected power/interference solves, search paths, catalogues, service and rate metrics, EE figures, calibration diagnostics at the frozen price, features, labels, learned models, trajectories, contrasts, intervals and admission decisions before carrying them into successor claims; reuse only demonstrably unaffected exogenous inputs and controls. Publish both rules, all widths, energy costs, user losses, caps, failures and negative signs, including the simple-versus-strict numerical distinction, and report the current full-width strict comparison as uncompleted until it exists. Disclose the shared commissioning and assumptions of the reviews, the nominal/full-buffer service semantics, the scalar/dense service discrepancy, repeated-observation denominators, TRAIN-only panels and bounded-search limitations; claim neither 90% network availability nor guaranteed target delivery from the quantile identity. Any later confirmation must follow a prospectively frozen protocol on the reserved unused confirmation data, with unchanged acceptance criteria and failures reported in full.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/PARAMETRISATION-COMPARISON-2026-09-10.md:13:The corpus combines the read-only mechanism corpus `/home/sat/mcrl-v025-coalgen-ws/artifacts/v025-mechanism-coalition-corpus-20260909-PILOT_NOT_CLAIM` with exact large S0 catalogue rows generated locally. The mechanism rows contribute sizes 2–6; the added rows contribute size 100. Selection is evaluated against the exact best row in each held-out anchor's same labelled pool. These are legal, exactly evaluated catalogue/mechanism proposals; no additional service-guard filter was invented. The pre-existing corpus does not carry a per-row served-count receipt, so this experiment neither reapplies nor alters that guard.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:9:4. **Labels:** C1 whole-network surplus + Φ (bits / κ); C2 three-offset forecast core with −κ per absorbing lost offset (bits / κ); C3 interaction share only (Ψ/2 pairs; Shapley for sets) over the sealed bounded catalogue; κ per stage-4 item 24; all prices explicit.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v0-2026-09-08.md:16:9. **Deployed selector:** per-user masked argmax of the normalised Q1 + Q2 sum (bits / κ) for the two-head policy; the C3 layer is the set-level coordinator (learned S3 or exact S0) over the bounded catalogue with the sealed service guard, a 30.08 s deadline, BASE-proposal fallback, and the deployment-capability manifest (stage-4 item 26); the information-matched `S_UNI` comparator is always evaluated beside it.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-retrain-ws/V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:7:**Scope:** quarantined development worlds only (`V025_PROBE/world/{1,2}` for training rows, `world/{3,4}` for evaluation), the engine as it stands at the stage-4d/4f snapshot with the fixed provider, 30 anchors per world per carrier, the sealed catalogue and arms, **4 learner seeds** and the sealed learner configuration, 6 arms.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:9:The scorer is physics-free by design. Its second input is an authenticated scoring-panel JSON that owns the common ordered catalogue, model inputs, declared full-buffer physical outcomes, fixed-point certificate identity, and 10 s anytime-incumbent identity. This separation prevents model loss, training data, or synthetic targets from being treated as EE evidence. It also makes the same checkpoint and anchor inventory feed both axes.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:17:- `F8-recovered-fraction.csv`: each arm's pooled EE fraction of the certified fixed point, with the 10 s anytime incumbent beside it.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:25:The primary comparison is exactly `FULL - ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL`. `BASE` appears only as a panel catalogue start/fallback identity; it is never an arm, statistical reference, or alias for the neutral control. Route rows are `FULL - DROP_C1`, `FULL - DROP_C2`, and `FULL - DROP_C3`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:27:Axis B reports `pooled EE_arm / pooled EE_certified-fixed-point`. It also reports the anytime incumbent obtained at the same 10 s wall-clock budget, its fixed-point fraction, and `arm - anytime`. The certified object is explicitly offline; it is not substituted for the anytime comparator.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:38:For every checkpoint and anchor, the scorer selects `ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL` normally and separately applies an all-route deployed-score knockout to the `FULL` checkpoint. The knockout sets C1, C2, and C3 contributions to exact zero while preserving catalogue order and the tie rule. It is not added to the trained arm inventory.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:40:The output lists both committed profile identities, differing anchors, and the pooled EE difference on the same full-buffer numerator. Classification is global over all supplied checkpoints. If the two selections coincide at every anchor and checkpoint, every primary row is relabelled `knockout_contrast_no_source_substitution_claim`. Otherwise it is labelled `neutral_source_substitution_contrast_decision_separated_from_knockout`. This label is an interpretation; the equality/difference inputs are executed results.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:46:- `panel_identity`: nonempty name, information class, estimand, the exact full-buffer numerator string, energy boundary, ordered anchor/world/date/world-seed inventories, provisioning rule, and explicit fixed-point traversal order;
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:50:- `anchors`: identities, the three profile references (`base`, certified fixed point, anytime incumbent), ordered profiles, and optional runner-recorded per-arm instrumentation;
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:51:- each profile: C1 and C2 selected/reference state pairs, C3 coalition size and invariant state, and a physical outcome containing full-buffer bits, joules, and additive co-metric counts.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:53:Model-input widths are checked against all five checkpoint arms. Reference profile identities must exist in each anchor catalogue. Energy must be positive; counts must be nonnegative and numerators may not exceed their denominators. The panel must attest `full_buffer_no_demand_cap: true`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/DUAL-AXIS-SCORER-2026-09-10.md:112:Verified by running code: supplied runner/checkpoint hashes; checkpoint decoding; five-arm inventory; three-anchor smoke selection; full-buffer pooling; F6/F7/F8 row counts and files; knockout execution; null acceleration instrumentation; progress lines; niceness/thread receipt; 71,094,272-byte peak RSS; three focused tests.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:1:**On the loaded one-worker machine, the deployed five-arm path took 12.014 s median and 24.079 s worst case per anchor against the 10 s budget, and catalogue construction dominated.**
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:21:The benchmark follows the deployed scalar path in [`run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1503–1578`](scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py#L1503): action deltas, contexts only for changed-set size at least two, additive-plus-interaction catalogue scores, and stable configuration-ID tie-breaking. It measures five arms: `FULL`, `DROP_C1`, `DROP_C2`, `DROP_C3`, and `ALL_NEUTRAL_CONTROL`.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:25:- The deployed action-head path does not forward every catalogue row independently. It computes reusable deltas from exactly 2,900 `(user, action)` rows per anchor. Because the production loop re-forwards candidate and reference through both Q1 and Q2, this is **58,000 scalar action-head forwards per anchor** across five arms, 1,160,000 over the panel.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:54:`Ctx miss` is the fraction of legal catalogue rows for which `contexts.get(...) is None`. `Other` is the explicitly measured eligibility filter + stable argmax + commit bookkeeping + unassigned wrapper overhead; its components remain separate in the receipt and distribution table.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:56:| anchor | rows | rows×5 | contexts | ctx miss | features | catalogue | contexts | heads | assemble | physical | other | total | §F2 |
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:81:There were 4,211 context-bearing rows and 15,569 context-free rows among 19,780 legal catalogue rows. The pooled `contexts.get(...) is None` fraction was **78.7108%**. Across anchors it was min / q25 / median / q75 / max / mean = **78.1347% / 78.5729% / 78.7769% / 78.9014% / 79.1751% / 78.7079%**. This is 0.4532 percentage points below the supplied C3REACH value of 79.164% and confirms the same sparse interaction-forward regime.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:118:- With catalogue construction removed, all observed remaining work was 3.262–6.352 s per anchor (median 3.715 s). This identifies catalogue construction as the necessary first optimization target; it does not claim that removal is contract-admissible.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:122:The acceleration claim's latency prerequisite is **not live for the current deployed five-arm path on this loaded machine**. The learned forward passes are not the problem: all five arms' heads took 0.445 s median. `_catalogue_with_census` is the bottleneck: 8.299 s median, 19.184 s worst, and by itself exhausted the contract on nine anchors.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/SELECTOR-LATENCY-2026-09-10.md:124:To make the prerequisite live without changing §F2, catalogue generation—especially its exact nominal unilateral ranking/evaluation—must be made materially faster, then the full presentation-to-commit distribution must be rerun with the real deployable checkpoint and runner-enforced cancellation. The observed total needs at least **2.014 s** reduction at the median and **14.079 s** at the worst anchor; for all 20 observed anchors, catalogue time would have to fit the 3.648–6.738 s residual allowance left by their other work. Batching/vectorising or safely caching the repeated nominal ranking work is the evident engineering seam. Moving catalogue construction outside the timer would require an explicit timing-contract/provisioning amendment and equal treatment of the comparator; it cannot be assumed after seeing this result.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws/CEILING30-MARGIN-2026-09-10.md:5:This is a separate diagnostic evaluation on copied code. No sealed constant, source artefact, frozen manifest, sign, seed, horizon, price, service guard, cap, catalogue rule, or acceptance rule was changed. There was no training run, learner, or policy run.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-ceiling30-ws/CEILING30-MARGIN-2026-09-10.md:140:This result compares two provisioning formulations; it does not rank or recommend either one. `UNILATERAL` remains a deterministic path-dependent coordinate-wise optimum, not a global optimum. `ORACLE_SET` remains the best exact-objective result only within the unchanged bounded hand-built catalogue, so its gain is catalogue-specific coordination headroom rather than a global coordination ceiling.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:6:2. **§C2 — feature sufficiency for the set-conditioned head.** The encoder's input must contain, for the changed-user set and its affected beams: proposed and incumbent associations by physical identity, background occupancy and activation before and after insertion, the shared-resource relations among the affected beams, and the **pairwise cross-gain terms among the affected beams** (not only a scalar interference summary — a summary can hide exactly the difference that flips a coupled fixed point). Acceptance test T2 is extended: the information-twin pair must be separable with the full context and provably ambiguous when the cross-gain block is removed.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:7:3. **§C4 / report schema — honest axes for a learned S3.** Over one catalogue that is exactly evaluated, S3 cannot exceed S0's maximum of the same score; therefore the only admissible learned claims are (i) better realised closed-loop pooled EE under model mismatch, (ii) equal decision quality at materially lower measured end-to-end computation, or (iii) a measured residual task (search allocation, evaluation-count reduction). The claim axis is named before training. A learned escape proposer over a wider neighbourhood is **not** part of this study; it may be proposed later with its own declaration and only if profiling shows evaluation is the bottleneck.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.2-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:9:5. **Report schema — anti-pattern statistics (round 9D).** The terminal report must contain, per contrast: net collision-avoidance value with both components unclipped; the additive-reversal frequency and whether the coordinator prevents them; escape recall and harmful-acceptance rate stratified by coalition size; top-choice agreement between the learned and exact selectors; the full decision-latency distribution including feature construction, catalogue generation, physics-call count, timeout frequency and fallback-inclusive outcomes; and the four experiments of §C3 reported separately and never interchanged.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/RESEEDED-SPAN-2026-09-10.md:113:The converged `U_first` assignments were reused from the completed anytime receipts, produced by the exact first-improvement implementation digest `003bdee1df908fddf652f2f8069c31a6297a7f7178bbb83338d09b3f4add9928`. `U_best`, `J_from_best`, and the neutral baseline were reconstructed from the archived standing-harness receipts. The new run rebuilt and exhausted the joint catalogue independently from each seed; no deadline was applied.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/RESEEDED-SPAN-2026-09-10.md:138:No learner, training, policy, tuning, new local-search order, new catalogue family, expanded cap, changed guard, statistical inference, or timing claim was attempted. This diagnostic covers only the fixed twenty anchors and the two existing provisioning rules. It does not revisit the five-point beam-width curve or thirty-date interval; their coordination quantities remain stale until recomputed with correctly paired seeds. No sealed artefact or frozen manifest was modified.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/V025-STAGES-6-8-CONTRACT-v1.1-AMENDMENT-2026-09-09.md:17:4. Everything else in v1 stands. Remaining `CONTROLLER_DECIDE` from build 3 (coalition feature scales, neutral-source seals, catalogue CB-2 construction, formal allocation manifest, operational capability values, causal operational variant) are seal-time items resolved with the launch package and the stage-C spec v1 seal.
