/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/EVAL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:219:Top single line by self time is `batch.py:77(_evaluate_ar_tdm_catalogue_core)` at 36.85 s of 48.07 s; everything else is numpy reduction machinery called from inside it.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/EVAL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:231:Structurally: a tape is built by `probe.build_world_tape` from the provider alone, before any evaluator object exists in the call graph, and a variant only ever replaces `probe.evaluate_ar_tdm_catalogue`. Empirically as well —
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/EVAL-HARNESS-2026-09-10.md:275:**The 94.5 % inside `_evaluate_ar_tdm_catalogue_core` cannot be cached, and no amount of engineering will change that.** It is precisely the quantity the provisioning rule alters. Worse than that, the variant changes the selector's *path*: `MARGIN_Q` reaches different unilateral optima, so it does not even visit the same set of configurations. There is no shared sub-result between `SEALED` and `MARGIN_Q` at the configuration level to memoise.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-selector-ws/V025-PILOT-TRACK-DECLARATION-2026-09-09.md:7:**Scope:** quarantined development worlds only (`V025_PROBE/world/{1,2}` for training rows, `world/{3,4}` for evaluation), the engine as it stands at the stage-4d/4f snapshot with the fixed provider, 30 anchors per world per carrier, the sealed catalogue and arms, **4 learner seeds** and the sealed learner configuration, 6 arms.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/ANYTIME-UNILATERAL-2026-09-10.md:9:Most of the prize is available before the deadline under both provisioning rules. By 20 seconds the first-improvement search has already obtained 69.51% (`SEALED`) and 77.03% (`MARGIN_Q`) of its eventual pooled gain; by 30.08 seconds those fractions are 81.74% and 87.85%. Therefore the proposed argument—*the converged exact search misses the interval, so a learned method may claim the within-interval win*—fails on this panel. A learned method would need to beat the actual anytime incumbent at the same wall-clock budget, not the legal base configuration or a convergence certificate time.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/ANYTIME-UNILATERAL-2026-09-10.md:11:First-improvement changed the local-search path and the fixed point on all 20 anchors under both rules. Its converged pooled EE is 8.13% above the archived best-improvement endpoint under `SEALED` and 1.62% above it under `MARGIN_Q`. Accordingly, every prize fraction below is shown against both endpoints where relevant.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/ANYTIME-UNILATERAL-2026-09-10.md:228:A seed at 10, 20, or 30.08 seconds consumes that much of the same budget. Only unilateral cache entries completed by the seed time are reusable. The current joint catalogue requires a physically best alternative for every user, so completing that alternate sweep and building the catalogue is charged to joint time. Joint candidates are evaluated in batches of 32; only completed batches can change the incumbent. At 30.08 seconds no joint time remains.
