/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/ANYTIME-UNILATERAL-2026-09-10.md:296:Best-improvement completes each user's whole neighbourhood and takes its best move. First-improvement commits the first strict improvement in sealed option order and skips the rest of that user's neighbourhood. Both are strict monotone coordinate searches, but their move sequences enter different local basins. Here first-improvement is not merely a scheduling optimization: it changes every fixed point and happens to improve the pooled committed endpoint under both rules. The archived endpoints remain the exact 20/20 matched control.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-harness-ws/ANYTIME-UNILATERAL-2026-09-10.md:319:No learned method was run, so this does not establish that exact search wins the interval; it establishes the comparator the learned method must beat. No repeated timing trials or confidence intervals were run. The `SEALED` best-improvement control contains the disclosed OS-scheduling outlier, so its raw mean is not a clean algorithmic runtime estimate. The joint search was not redesigned: it retains the archived physically-best-alternative prerequisite and bounded mechanism catalogue, with only deadline-aware batching. World-tape construction was not charged per decision because the standing harness defines the immutable tape as the decision input; all decision-local feature and candidate construction was charged. No sealed file or frozen manifest was modified.
